{"id":49040,"ord":39,"n_segments":324,"prev":49039,"next":49041,"doc":{"id":"61539","title":"61539_Butter Jackson oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Quentin Jackson","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/61539/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=61539"},"chapter":"Cab Calloway's band","title":"The Calloway trombone and reed sections he joined","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"The section was Keg Johnson, Tyree Glenn and Jackson; he lists the trumpets and saxophones, with Hilton Jefferson replacing Chauncey Houghton.","period":"1940","year_from":1940,"year_to":1940,"words":149,"start":[46,14],"end":[48,1],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=61539#s49040","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Cab Calloway Orchestra","focus":1,"leader":"Cab Calloway"}]},"people":[{"name":"Tyree Glenn","qid":"Q488323","n":2},{"name":"Claude Jones","qid":"Q1096827","n":2},{"name":"Hilton Jefferson","qid":"Q282977","n":2},{"name":"Jerry Blake","qid":"Q1687800","n":2},{"name":"Chauncey Haughton","qid":"Q133644248","n":2},{"name":"Dizzy Gillespie","qid":"Q49575","n":1},{"name":"Lamar Wright","qid":"Q1801588","n":1},{"name":"A. J. Brown","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Chu Berry","qid":"Q1089014","n":1},{"name":"Walter Thomas","qid":"Q1645240","n":1},{"name":"Mario Bauza","qid":"Q722618","n":1}],"story":{"theme":34,"theme_name":"Who was in the band: naming sidemen and personnel","community":60,"community_name":"Who played in the band: reciting personnel","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":46,"b":14,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"And we worked out a very good section"},{"p":47,"b":0,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"because we was all, you know, friends, you know. And in fact in that band everybody was friends, you know."},{"p":47,"b":1,"s":"MR. ________","x":"So it was Claude Jones -- ?"},{"p":47,"b":2,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"No, Claude had left."},{"p":47,"b":3,"s":"MR. ________","x":"No. Keg --"},{"p":47,"b":4,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"And Tyree and myself."},{"p":47,"b":5,"s":"MR. ________","x":"-- and Tyree."},{"p":47,"b":6,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"We only had three. That's right. And the trombones was Lamar Wright and Mario Bauza and Dizzy."},{"p":47,"b":7,"s":"MR. ________","x":"Oh, yeah."},{"p":47,"b":8,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"You see?"},{"p":47,"b":9,"s":"MR. ________","x":"Right. (Laughter)"},{"p":47,"b":10,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"And Chauncey was leaving when I came in the band. Chauncey was leaving and Hilton Jefferson came in."},{"p":47,"b":11,"s":"MR. ________","x":"Oh, yeah. (Candy)"},{"p":47,"b":12,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"You see, because Brown was still there and Foots was still there and Chu was there and Jacinto Chabania."},{"p":47,"b":13,"s":"MR. ________","x":"Yeah, Jerry Blake."},{"p":47,"b":14,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"Jerry Blake."},{"p":47,"b":15,"s":"MR. ________","x":"The baritone sax player. Let's see, you say -- let me get this straight. I was wondering, who was leaving as Jeff came in?"},{"p":47,"b":16,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"Chauncey Houghton."},{"p":48,"b":0,"s":"MR. ________","x":"Oh, yeah, that's right, right."},{"p":48,"b":1,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"Yeah."}]}